      "lineStart": 125,
      "lineEnd": 127,
      "severity": "important",
      "category": "correctness",
      "title": "stderr captured into $head makes the empty-repo branch unreachable",
      "description": "`Invoke-Native` merges stderr into its output (`2>&1 | Out-String`), so in a repository with no commits `git rev-parse --short HEAD` returns the text \"fatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD'...\" rather than an empty string. `if ($head)` is then truthy and the script prints \"it has commits (fatal: ambiguous argument 'HEAD'…)\"; the \"no commits yet\" warning can never fire.",
      "suggestion": "Consider validating the output shape before treating it as a sha, e.g. match against `^[0-9a-f]{4,40}$`.",
      "confidence": 0.88,
      "hadPatch": true,
      "status": "proposed",
      "accepted": false,
      "dismissReason": null,
      "detectedBy": "llm"
    },
    {
      "id": "f2",
      "file": "selfhost/doctor.ps1",
      "lineStart": 104,
      "lineEnd": 106,
      "severity": "nit",
      "category": "correctness",
      "title": "a failing `claude --version` is reported as success",
      "description": "Same stderr-merging behaviour: if the binary exists but errors (missing DLL, bad install), `Invoke-Native` returns the error text, `$ver` is non-empty, and the doctor prints \"reports: <error text>\" as an ok line without incrementing `$script:problems` — exactly the case this section exists to catch.",
      "suggestion": "Consider requiring the output to look like a version (e.g. `$ver -match '\\d+\\.\\d+'`) before treating it as a pass.",
